    autresNoms: "Linda problem, Erreur de conjonction",
    definition: "Judging that a combination of two events is more probable than one of them alone, which is mathematically impossible.",
    mecanisme: "We judge probability by resemblance to a stereotype (the representativeness heuristic). A more detailed scenario seems more plausible because it is more coherent, whereas each added detail lowers its probability: P(A and B) ≤ P(A).",
