    cas: "Presented as having “a 90% five-year survival rate”, a treatment is accepted by most patients. Presented as having “10% five-year mortality”, it is refused by many of them.",
    cas2: "A doctor is far more inclined to prescribe a drug presented as “reducing the risk of heart attack by 50%” than a drug “taking that risk from 2% to 1%”, although both formulations describe the same effect.",
    casSup: ["One petrol station advertises “5 cents off per litre for cash payment”. Another, with the same prices, advertises “a 5-cent surcharge per litre for card payment”. Customers find the second far more unfair.",
      "A town hall presents a project as “saving 200 jobs out of 600”; another presentation says “cutting 400 jobs out of 600”. Residents approve of the first far more."],
