    autresNoms: "Default effect, Biais du statu quo",
    definition: "Preferring the current situation or the default option, even when an alternative would be more advantageous.",
    mecanisme: "Change involves effort, uncertainty and the risk of regret. Because of loss aversion, the drawbacks of change weigh more than its advantages.",
    exemple: "Keeping the same electricity supplier for years without ever comparing offers.",
    cas: "A company offers a retirement savings plan. When enrolment is automatic (with the option to opt out), 90% of employees take part; when people have to sign up themselves, fewer than half do.",
